icture leaves black bars above and below. Fill zooms in to cover the TV and cuts off the left and right edges; a 16:9 video then fills the TV exactly. Mac screens are never cropped. While mirroring, press Up or Down to switch.</string><string name="fit_value">Fit whole picture</string><string name="fill_value">Fill the screen</string><string name="fill_hint">Black bars? Press Up to fill the screen</string><string name="fill_on">Filling the screen (sides cut off). Up or Down to go back.</string><string name="fill_off">Whole picture. Up or Down to fill the screen.</string><string name="setting_sound">Sound</string><string name="setting_sound_hint">Play the mirrored device’s sound on the TV</string><string name="setting_stats">Show stats while mirroring</string><string name="setting_stats_hint">You can also press OK on the remote while mirroring</string><string name="setting_background">Stay visible after closing the app</string><string name="setting_background_hint">Keeps the TV in Screen Mirroring lists while you use other apps</string><string name="setting_diagnostics">Diagnostics</string><string name="setting_diagnostics_hint">What the TV detected and offers, plus the recent AirPlay log. Useful when reporting a problem.</string><string name="view">View</string><string name="on">On</string><string name="off">Off</string><string name="overlay_title">Allow the player to open by itself?</string><string name="setting_background_needs_overlay">Visible, but Android won’t let the player open by itself while another app is on screen. Run this once from your Mac: %1$s</string><string name="overlay_message">To start mirroring while another app is open, Android needs Mango Screen Cast For macOS/iOS to have “Display over other apps” permission. If this TV has no settings screen for it, run this once from your Mac:\n\n%1$s</string><string name="overlay_open">Open settings</string><string name="overlay_later">Not now</string><string name="about">Mango Screen Cast For macOS/iOS %1